{
  "dom_id": "step-q126743",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find a vector that's tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{3t+2},2t-5⟩$ at the point where $t=-1.$",
  "worked_solution": "At the point where $t=-1,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(-1)$ is tangent to the curve.\n\nLet's calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t+2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{3t+2},2⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨3{e}^{3(-1)+2},2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{-1},2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=-1$ is $⟨3{e}^{-1},2⟩.$",
